  "articleBody": "Small nail holes are simple weekend fixes, but extensive drywall finishing quickly demands specialized tools and experienced hands. Here are clear signs it is time to bring in a finish contractor for your walls.\n\n- Extensive surface areas: Sanding entire basements, room additions, or multiple rooms by hand creates severe fatigue and uneven wall planes.\n- High ceilings and tall walls: Reaching elevated seams safely requires sturdy scaffolding, specialized pole sanders, and experienced balance.\n- Damaged drywall paper: If underlying drywall paper has torn or frayed, improper sanding will ruin the finish coat without professional skim-coating.\n- Strict dust control needs: If your family lives in the home during remodeling, you need tight containment, proper respirators, and HEPA vacuum cleanup.\n- Demanding paint-ready standards: Rooms with large windows and direct natural light expose every tiny ridge or dip if seams are not feathered completely flush.\n\nWhen Professional Guidance Helps\nAn experienced finish contractor ensures joint compound is properly cured, leveled, and cleaned before primer goes on. To schedule reliable drywall sanding and interior renovation work, get in touch with Abraham Becerra at HH Remodeling LLC by calling 303-505-0866.",
  "datePublished": "2026-10-23"
